"""The links on a bot's page: which service each one points to, its icon and a default label.

An owner's links are `{label, url}` items (the card stores nothing else). The service is read from the URL's host,
so the icon always says where a link really goes, whatever its label says. An address with no known service gets a
globe; `mailto:` and `tel:` links get an envelope and a phone.

The brand marks are monochrome paths from Simple Icons (CC0 1.0, https://simpleicons.org), except LinkedIn's, which is
from Bootstrap Icons (MIT, https://icons.getbootstrap.com). Each brand belongs to its owner; the marks only show where
a link leads. Pure functions only (stdlib): used by the gateway (checks, the page) and the client (labels, input).
"""
